From: VintagePomeloPro (migrated from main branch ad7bdd7f092)
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: allow disabling GDI text antialiasing per process

Legacy titles render text with GDI into an offscreen bitmap and then threshold
that bitmap into a 1-bit glyph mask (the GGE/XYQ private-server clients keep
only pixels above 0x7ffe as ink). Grayscale antialiasing turns most of a 12px
CJK stroke grey, so the mask keeps only stroke cores and every in-game string
falls apart into scattered fragments that read like mojibake.

Add WINEHUA_FONT_AA=bitmap|gray, read once per process, so game processes can
request bilevel glyphs while the Wine desktop keeps the grayscale default.
The app side (WineEngineService) already pushes WINEHUA_FONT_AA=bitmap for
game launches on this branch; this patch adds the wine-side reader so the
override takes effect. Migrated from main-branch wine commit ad7bdd7f092
(24bbc2b3 "fix(compat): render legacy GDI game text without antialiasing");
context offsets adapted to the wine-valve baseline.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/font.c b/dlls/win32u/font.c
index dcc75e8096b..9c29f498e42 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -4517,6 +4517,44 @@ static struct gdi_font *select_font( LOGFONTW *lf, FMAT2 dcmat, BOOL can_use_bit
     return font;
 }
 
+/*************************************************************
+ *           ohos_font_aa_override
+ *
+ * Per-process override for GDI text antialiasing.
+ *
+ * A large family of legacy CJK (and western) titles renders text with GDI into
+ * an offscreen bitmap and then thresholds that bitmap into a 1-bit glyph mask -
+ * e.g. the popular GGE/XYQ private-server clients keep only pixels above
+ * 0x7ffe as ink. Grayscale antialiasing turns most of a 12px CJK stroke grey,
+ * so the mask keeps only stroke cores and the rendered text falls apart into
+ * scattered fragments.
+ *
+ * Game processes can therefore ask for bilevel glyphs without changing the
+ * desktop appearance:
+ *
+ *     WINEHUA_FONT_AA=bitmap -> GGO_BITMAP      (no antialiasing)
+ *     WINEHUA_FONT_AA=gray   -> GGO_GRAY4_BITMAP
+ */
+static UINT ohos_font_aa_override(void)
+{
+#ifdef __OHOS__
+    static int cached = -1;
+
+    if (cached < 0)
+    {
+        const char *value = getenv( "WINEHUA_FONT_AA" );
+
+        cached = 0;
+        if (value && !strcmp( value, "bitmap" )) cached = GGO_BITMAP;
+        else if (value && !strcmp( value, "gray" )) cached = GGO_GRAY4_BITMAP;
+        TRACE( "OHOS font AA override env=%s -> %#x\n", value ? value : "(unset)", cached );
+    }
+    return cached;
+#else
+    return 0;
+#endif
+}
+
 /*************************************************************
  * font_SelectFont
  */
@@ -4543,6 +4581,12 @@ static HFONT font_SelectFont( PHYSDEV dev, HFONT hfont, UINT *aa_flags )
             break;
         }
 
+        {
+            UINT forced_aa = ohos_font_aa_override();
+
+            if (forced_aa) *aa_flags = forced_aa;
+        }
+
         if (lf.lfOutPrecision == OUT_TT_ONLY_PRECIS)
             can_use_bitmap = FALSE;
 
